      "text": "To find the mean, we first need to find the value of \\( n \\). We know that the median of the set is 9. In a sorted set, the median is the middle number. Since there are five numbers in the set, the median will be the third number in the sorted order.\n\nGiven the set \\(\\{n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15\\}\\), the third number in some sorted order will be \\( n+6 \\). Hence, we set up the equation:\n\\[ n+6 = 9 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\\[ n+6 = 9 \\]\n\\[ n = 9 - 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 3 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( n \\), we can find the mean of the set. The mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. The set \\(\\{n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15\\}\\) becomes \\(\\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\}\\) when \\( n = 3 \\). Therefore, the mean is:\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{3+8+9+12+18}{5} = \\frac{50}{5} = 10 \\]\n\nHere is the Python code to verify this result:\n\n```python\n# Define the value of n\nn = 9 - 6\n\n# Given set of numbers\nnumbers = [n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15]\n\n# Calculate the mean\nmean = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\nprint(mean)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe mean of the set \\(\\{n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15\\}\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
